# Line-ending policy for the pack.
# The bash tools and PACK_DIGEST.txt sha256 hashes assume LF; a CRLF working
# tree breaks Linux CI and the digest. Normalize text to LF in the index and in
# checkouts. See HYG-P2-001 and docs/OBSERVABILITY.md.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf

# Generated-inventory merge policy.
# PACK_DIGEST.txt hashes the whole tree, so any two PRs that each change a file
# conflict on it and every rebase means regenerating it by hand. Let a merge keep
# one side for this file (`merge=ours`) and let the push-to-main workflow
# (.github/workflows/pack-digest.yml) regenerate the single source of truth.
# `ours` is NOT a built-in driver: each clone must enable it once with
#   git config merge.ours.driver true
# (helper: tools/setup_git_merge_driver.sh). Without the driver Git falls back to
# a normal 3-way merge, so this line is harmless in CI/fork clones that never
# configure it. See CONTRIBUTING.md, "Generated digest".
PACK_DIGEST.txt merge=ours
